---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About – BRIC.News" description="Editorial mission, correction policy, and takedown policy for BRIC.News.">
  <section class="module-band bg-bone">
    <div class="container-content max-w-prose">
      <h1 class="font-heading font-extrabold text-4xl md:text-5xl text-charcoal mb-6">About BRIC.News</h1>

      <h2 class="font-heading font-bold text-brick text-xl mt-10 mb-3">Our mission</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        BRIC.News exists to help Columbus-metro real estate investors and landlords get work done and stay informed. We track policy changes across Central Ohio municipalities, surface local market news, maintain a curated directory of vendors Columbus investors use, and compile the resources you'd otherwise have to hunt down yourself.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Our editorial standards are simple: Columbus-first framing, primary sources, specific numbers, no hype. If we don't know something, we say so. If we get something wrong, we correct it.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-4">
        We don't take sponsorship for news coverage. Vendor directory listings are free. Preferred designations are editorial picks based on stated criteria, not paid placements. If you think we got one wrong, tell us.
      </p>

      <h2 id="corrections" class="font-heading font-bold text-brick text-xl mt-12 mb-3">Correction policy</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        If you find a factual error in any item, email <a href="mailto:corrections@bric.news">corrections@bric.news</a> with the item URL and what needs to change. We review every correction request within seven days. If the correction is factually supported we make the fix and note the change at the bottom of the item.
      </p>

      <h2 id="takedown" class="font-heading font-bold text-brick text-xl mt-12 mb-3">Vendor takedown policy</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Any vendor can request removal from the directory at any time, for any reason. Email <a href="mailto:vendors@bric.news">vendors@bric.news</a> from the business email on the listing (or another verifiable channel) and we will remove the entry within seven days. This applies to every tier of listing, including Preferred designations.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact" class="font-heading font-bold text-brick text-xl mt-12 mb-3">Contact</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        General inquiries: <a href="mailto:hello@bric.news">hello@bric.news</a><br/>
        Corrections: <a href="mailto:corrections@bric.news">corrections@bric.news</a><br/>
        Vendor submissions and takedowns: <a href="mailto:vendors@bric.news">vendors@bric.news</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
